Hi,

I have a Broadcom BCM57781 NIC on a ASRock mobo and I've encountered
multiple times when the transmit queue times out and dumps the output
which can be seen with dmesg. This appears to happen when I download
at high speeds (~ 3 MiB/s). If I turn off TSO with ethtool -K enp3s0
tso off, the problem seems to go away. If I replace this NIC with a
Realtek one, the problem does not happen so it appears this is somehow
specific to the Broadcom NIC. I've tried another NIC with the same
BCM57781 chip, and it happens too. Any clues?


